# The shard checks a claim's raise and a stamped append against the leaf's
# entry only, not the retired floor. A claim written before a purge and
# re-creation of the leaf is raised after it, because the retirement reset the
# entry, so an epoch the old incarnation already superseded appends.
MODULE: StaleEpochNeverAppendsIgnoresRetiredFloor
TARGET: StaleEpochNeverAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: neither the claim's raise nor a stamped append is refused at or below the retired floor
PERTURBS: ClaimRaise, OwnAlloc
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= Max2(fence, memFence)
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the raise.
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
    /\ epoch[a] > retired
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ epoch[a] >= memFence
\* MUTATION: the retired floor is not checked at the append.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END